{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself spices.</b> Our earlier predecessors, of blessed memory, received that there are eleven kinds of spices. Now, the verse says 'for spices' — they are for the incense of spices. The verse did not specify them, and it mentioned 'spices' because it did not state their weights." "The meaning of 'spices' elsewhere: 'these are spices' — and pure frankincense with them." "<b>Bead by bead.</b> Each one separately is compounded, and afterward they are mixed."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:28.889717045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}